  |_|                       |C|                       2 - Divine Water
                                                      3 - Mana Cape
   B5           B6           B7           B8          4 - Wind God Book
   _            _            _            _           5 - Mythril Mail
 _|E|          | |         _|F|          |H|          6 - Celestial Dew
|T  |          | | _      |_  |          | | _        7 - Tourniquet x2
 _| |_     ____| || |_     _| |_     ____| ||S|_      8 - Medibranch
|_    |   |E____ _XX_F|   |_    |   |_____ ____G|
  | |*|     |__   __|       | |_|     |7_   _*|
  |D|          |_|          |G|          |6|</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>B9             B10
      _          _         _
     |I|        | |   _   | |
     | | _      |  \_| |_/  |
 ____| || |_     \___   ___/
|*_XX_ _XX_8|        | |
  |__   __|          | |          Each letter (A-I) on the map teleports to its
     |H|             |I|          corresponding letter in the lab.</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <p>The path through this area is very straight-forward. Head up to an intersection and right to a chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Superior Teas</Tag>. Then, walk up to the teleporter to the next floor.</p>
      <p>Head right to an intersection and take the lower right path to a chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Divine Water</Tag>. Return to the intersection and follow the upper right path to the teleporter to the next floor.</p>
      <p>Go down to an intersection and search the area to the right for a hidden chest which contains the <Tag type="armor">Mana Cape</Tag> (DEF+21/MDF+68/SPD-3, sell). From the intersection, proceed down to the teleporter to the next floor.</p>
      <p>Walk left to a fork and search the upper area for a hidden chest which contains the <Tag type="key">Wind God Book</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag>. From the fork, head left to an intersection and take the lower left path. Pull the barricade out of the way to access a chest which contains a <Tag type="armor">Mythril Mail</Tag> (DEF+38/MDF+64/SPD-2, sell). Return to the intersection and continue left to the teleporter to the next floor.</p>
      <p>Proceed up to an intersection and search the right area for a hidden floor panel. Step on the switch to activate the next teleporter. From the intersection, head up, but hug the left wall until you can go through a path that is rather hard to see. Equip <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> with <Tag type="acc">Thauma Charms</Tag> and examine the thaumachine there.</p>
      <BossCard name="Special Thaumachine" weakness="Lightning">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Lay a <Tag type="skill">Volt Star Trap</Tag> behind him and <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> him onto it.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating it, you will receive the <Tag type="key">Blast Core</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag> and advance the [Thaumatech&#x27;s End] sidequest. Sadly, there is never a better time to turn in the quest than now, so I&#x27;d just recommend getting it out of the way. Walk all the way out of the lab and talk to the old man by the entrance to complete the [Thaumatech&#x27;s End] sidequest and receive a <Tag type="item">Medibranch</Tag>. It wouldn&#x27;t hurt to rest up at the inn, as long as you&#x27;re here. When you&#x27;re ready, return to the Underground Lab B5 and take the upper teleporter to the next floor.</p>
      <p>Head right to an intersection. Above and below you are two barrels that you will need to pull to blow away the blockade to the right. Once you&#x27;ve gotten past them, continue right to the teleporter to the next floor.</p>
      <p>Hug the left wall until you can go through another hard to see path. Talk to the engineer to receive the [A Scholar&#x27;s Creed] sidequest. From the fork, go down and search the right path for a hidden barrel. Pull it around to the main path to blow away the machine blocking the teleporter to the next floor.</p>
      <p>Go left to the intersection and down to a hidden chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Celestial Dew</Tag>. Take the lower left path to find a chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Tourniquets</Tag>. Finally, head down the lower right path to find a hidden floor panel. Push the switch to activate the teleporter to the next floor up the center path.</p>
      <p>Along the lower left and lower right paths are two hidden barrels. However, there are four barricades to use them on. First, use them to blow up the right barricades to gain access to a chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Medibranch</Tag>. Teleport to the previous floor and back to make the barrels respawn. This time, use them to blow away the left barricades. Search the area beyond to find a hidden floor panel. Push the switch to activate the teleporter to the next floor up the center path.</p>
      <p>Walk up and talk to <Tag type="char">Hugo</Tag> to be prompted for a decision. Choosing to &quot;Take the power&quot; will unlock the [Hugo the Omnipotent] ending.</p>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Demigod">
        <p>Return to this node, and instead choose to &quot;Draw your sword.&quot; You&#x27;ll fight <Tag type="boss">Hugo</Tag>, but it will be pitifully easy. Use whatever you want.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Wielder of Infinity">
        <p>Talk to <Tag type="char">Fennel</Tag> and pick up the <Tag type="weapon">Old Magic Blade</Tag> above the save point. Before restoring the Historica, return to &quot;The Beginning&quot; node. Talk to Fennel in the lab next door to complete the [A Scholar&#x27;s Creed] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="key">Haste Core</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>Return to the &quot;Celestian War&quot; node. Talk to <Tag type="char">Sonja</Tag> to install those new Cores into Rosch&#x27;s Gauntlet and learn those new abilities. Then, talk to <Tag type="char">Elm</Tag> to restore the power of <Tag type="weapon">HISTORICA</Tag> (ATK+58/MAG+28/SPD+2) and unlock the [Blade&#x27;s Resurrection] node. I prefer having a better magic stat for <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>, but hold onto the sword for later. You can also return to &quot;Gafka &amp; the Scrolls&quot; to have <Tag type="char">Bergas</Tag> teach that new scroll to <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag> too.</p>
      <p>Return to the &quot;Demigod&quot; node. I would bring in <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag> for this round. Talk to <Tag type="char">Hugo</Tag> for a slightly more challenging battle.</p>
      <BossCard name="Hugo" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Hugo can summon two Alistel Officers, but they&#x27;re nothing to worry about. Have Aht lay any Star Trap behind Hugo, then use <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> and <Tag type="skill">Right Assault</Tag> on him. He&#x27;ll probably summon those officers now. Lay any Star Trap at the center of the grid. Then, use your new <Tag type="skill">Wind God Strike</Tag> to drag everyone onto the trap and a Right Assault to finish off Hugo. You could steal a <Tag type="acc">Venus Ring</Tag> (HP+70/MP+50) from him and repeat the fight to get an unlimited supply, but I don&#x27;t like HP/MP boosting rings.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: An End to Madness">
        <p>After defeating <Tag type="boss">Hugo</Tag>, it appears that we have finally brought peace to <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag>. OR DID WE?!</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 64 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch64"
    number={64}
    title="Granorg (Alternate Final Chapter)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="65" party="Stocke, Aht, Rosch"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Shadow Crown">
        <p>While the shops don&#x27;t sell anything new, head east to the weapon shop. Talk to the nearby man in green to receive the [A Timely Warning] sidequest. Return to the &quot;Flux War&quot; node and advance the plot until you reach <Tag type="place">Granorg</Tag> again. Talk to him again to advance the [A Timely Warning] sidequest. Return to &quot;The Shadow Crown&quot; node, talk to him again to complete the [A Timely Warning] sidequest, and receive the <Tag type="key">Omnipedia Book</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag>. You can return to the &quot;Gafka &amp; the Scrolls&quot; node to teach that to him. When you are ready, return to &quot;The Shadow Crown&quot; node, walk up to <Tag type="place">Granorg Palace</Tag>, and talk to <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Heiss' Scheme">
        <p>You will need to head to the <Tag type="place">Imperial Ruins</Tag> via <Tag type="place">Judgement Cliff</Tag>. Along the way, make a pit stop at the <Tag type="place">Sand Fortress South</Tag>, where the merchant has some new wares, including a <Tag type="weapon">Mythril Edge</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
      <ShopMatrix title="Traveling Merchant" items={[{"name": "Soothing Balm      100     Mythril Edge", "price": 12400, "note": "buy for Stocke"}, {"name": "First Aid Kit      400     Mythril Spear", "price": 8600}, {"name": "Tourniquet        1000     Prayer Claw", "price": 7600}, {"name": "Herbal Tea         350     Mythril Dagger", "price": 14500}, {"name": "Special Tea       1200     Freikugel Mistel", "price": 12000}, {"name": "Superior Tea      2500     Grace Mail", "price": 3100}, {"name": "Healing Herb       500     Moonlight Cape", "price": 4200}, {"name": "Holy Water         500     Diana Dress", "price": 7300}, {"name": "Anti-Poison         50     Beast Charm", "price": 5000}, {"name": "Anti-Fear           50     Thauma Charm", "price": 5000}, {"name": "Anti-Paralytic      50     Rook Stud", "price": 6000}, {"name": "Anti-Curse          50     Arbor Ring", "price": 25000}, {"name": "Anti-Sleep", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Stone", "price": 50}, {"name": "Panacea", "price": 800}, {"name": "Panacea Plus", "price": 2000}, {"name": "Poison Wing", "price": 350}, {"name": "Sleep Wing", "price": 500}, {"name": "Power Down", "price": 500}, {"name": "Guard Down", "price": 500}, {"name": "Might Herb", "price": 500}, {"name": "Shield Herb", "price": 500}, {"name": "Divine Water", "price": 1500}]} itemTitle="Inventory" />
      <p>Continue on to <Tag type="place">Judgement Cliff</Tag>. Go south and west one screen. Use the barrel to blow away the rocks above to the exit to the <Tag type="place">Imperial Ruins</Tag>.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Mythril Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Moirae Manteau</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Thauma Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">La Tormenta</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Diamond Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Thauma Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Gaia Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Diamond Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Queen Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Rosch:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Death Pike</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Diamond Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Beast Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Glaux Dagger</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Giant Cape</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Queen Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Gafka:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Beast Claw</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Mighty Protector</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Beast Charm x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

