      </AsciiMap>
      <p>In the upper right corner of the area are two barrels. If you want to get the last of the treasure, you will have to drag both of them all the way to the beginning of the area. I would use them on the rocks in the upper right corner first, to access a hidden chest which contains the <Tag type="key">Soul Pact</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>. There is another chest in the lower right corner which contains a <Tag type="acc">Sky Armlet</Tag> (SPD+10) though you would have to leave and come back to make the barrels respawn. When you are ready, head to the next area via the upper exit.</p>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Black Guardians">
        <p>Before taking on the boss gauntlet, there are two hidden barrels in the lower left corner. Dragging them either directly up or right to blow away the rocks would prevent you from getting all the treasure in one go. Instead drag one up the middle and left to blow away the rocks blocking a chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Tourniquets</Tag>. Drag the other barrel up the middle and around to the right to blow away those rocks to gain access to a chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Superior Teas</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>Since unlocking a travel node, I would recommend finishing the last sidequest now. Return to the &quot;Gafka &amp; the Scrolls&quot; node to purchase <Tag type="acc">9 Sky Drops</Tag> (All resistances +2) and equip them on <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>, <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag>, and <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>. Rest up at an inn and return to &quot;The Three Contracts&quot; node. Teach the last of the Pacts to Stocke and <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag>. Talk to <Tag type="char">Vainqueur</Tag> again to receive [The Final Trial] sidequest. For these next battles, I would recommend using Stocke, Eruca, and Marco. Talk to Vainqueur to begin the battle.</p>
      <BossCard name="Master's House" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> This first test is very easy. Use the <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> command to string together 6 consecutive turns. Then cast <Tag type="skill">Magic Rise</Tag>, <Tag type="skill">Spin Strike</Tag>, <Tag type="skill">G-Fire</Tag>, G-Fire, <Tag type="skill">G-Frost</Tag>, and G-Frost to defeat it.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating <Tag type="boss">Vainqueur</Tag>, you will have completed [The Final Trial] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="weapon">TRUE HISTORICA</Tag> (ATK+70/MAG+34/SPD+5). I still prefer the <Tag type="weapon">Mythril Edge</Tag> for its far greater magic boost. If you&#x27;re trying to complete every node, you should have completed 217/236 nodes. The rest are all automatic, assuming you&#x27;ve completed all the sidequests up to now.</p>
      <p>Rest up at an inn and return to &quot;The Black Guardians&quot; node. Bring in <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>, equipping the accessories you had before. Examine the black glow in the lower right corner for your first final boss.</p>
      <BossCard name="Palomides, Pure Ice x2" weakness="Lightning, Fire (duh)">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Have Marco use <Tag type="skill">Magic Rise</Tag>, Aht lay a <Tag type="skill">Volt Star Trap</Tag> behind <Tag type="boss">Palomides</Tag>, and Stocke use <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> to quickly defeat him. Then, use two <Tag type="skill">Will o&#x27; Wisps</Tag> to defeat the Pure Ices.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating them, you will unlock the [Death in Black] node. Examine the upper right black glow for your next challenge.</p>
      <BossCard name="Garland, Silent Soul x2" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Have Marco use <Tag type="skill">Magic Rise</Tag>, Aht lay any Star Trap in the very back row between the two Silent Souls, and Stocke use <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> on <Tag type="boss">Garland</Tag>. Then, use <Tag type="skill">Cross Star</Tag> and two <Tag type="skill">Heat Blades</Tag> on Garland, which will take out the two Silent Souls. <Tag type="skill">Dancing Death</Tag> and a <Tag type="skill">G-Fire</Tag> should finish off Garland.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating them, you will unlock the [Warlord in Black] node. Bring in <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag>. Then, examine the lower left black glow for another boss.</p>
      <BossCard name="Guardian" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Stocke and Raynie should use <Tag type="item">Magic Herbs</Tag> on themselves, while Gafka uses <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> on the Guardian&#x27;s turn. Do so again to string together seven consecutive turns. Use 3 <Tag type="skill">Musous</Tag>, 2 <Tag type="skill">G-Fires</Tag>, and 2 <Tag type="skill">G-Thunders</Tag> for the win.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating it, you will unlock the [Monstrocity in Black] node. Examine the final black glow in the upper left corner for your final challenge.</p>
      <BossCard name="Floating Stone x2, Noble Flame x2, Viola" weakness="None, Ice, None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Use the <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> command to string together three turns: one for Gafka and two for Stocke. One <Tag type="skill">Musou</Tag> and two <Tag type="skill">Will o&#x27; Wisps</Tag> should defeat everyone except <Tag type="boss">Viola</Tag>. Another Musou and some G-elemental spells will defeat her.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating them, you will unlock the [Valkyrie in Black] node, as well as the door above, where you should go next.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Mythril Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Moirae Manteau</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Sky Drops x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">La Tormenta</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Diamond Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Sky Drops x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Gaia Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Diamond Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Sky Drops x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Rosch:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Der Lowe</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Diamond Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Sky Drops x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Glaux Dagger</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Giant Cape</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Sky Drops x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Gafka:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Beast Claw</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Mighty Protector</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Sky Drops x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Eruca:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Freikugel Mercy</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Luminous Dress</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Sky Drops x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Death Knell">
        <p>[Final Battleground node] As a reminder, you should have completed 223/236 nodes up to this point. It&#x27;s time for the final boss gauntlet. I would recommend using <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>, <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag>, and <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag>, preferably all with full Mana Burst gauges and at least Level 60. Recover with a <Tag type="item">Mana Crystal</Tag> at the save point and head up to save the world!</p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Black Chronicle, Shadow" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> The real target is the <Tag type="boss">Black Chronicle</Tag>. However, you cannot damage it, unless a Shadow is on the same tile with it. Use a <Tag type="item">Magic Herb</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag>, <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> the Shadow onto the Chronicle, and <Tag type="skill">G-Frost</Tag> for some decent damage. It will then summon more Shadows. Use the <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> command to string together five consecutive turns: two for Gafka and three for Eruca. Have Gafka use <Tag type="skill">Wind God Strike</Tag>, <Tag type="skill">Musou</Tag>, and Eruca cast three G-Frosts to defeat the Black Chronicle.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating Apocrypha, you will unlock the following nodes:</p>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Apocrypha">
        <p>[Ritual of Flux node] [A Promise node]</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>If you completed all of the sidequests, you will get some extra cutscenes during the ending and unlock even more nodes. I&#x27;ll go over them in more detail in the Node Completion List.</p>
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>[Iron-Armed General node]
[Shaman node]
[The Show Goes On node]
[A Little Hero node]
[Overseers of Time node]
[Valkyrie in Repose node]
[Beast God at Rest node]
[A Warrior in Love node]
[The Lives of Humans node]
[Life of the Beastkind node]</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <p>Congratulations on beating this awesome game! Sit back and enjoy the ending and well-deserved credits.</p>
      <p>The following is a complete list of how to unlock all 236 nodes in the game. They are sorted by chapter to make it easier to figure out which one(s) you are missing. This is probably best viewed when you are at the end of the game, as many of the node titles and their requirements contain extreme spoilers to the plot, and it would be difficult to sift through the entire main walkthrough for a handful of nodes. Furthermore, while you may get some sidequests very early in the game, they may not be completable until much later in the game. Finally, I will assume roadblocks are automatically resolved during the plot, as in that case, it&#x27;s simply easier to look up that section in the walkthrough.</p>
      <p>PROLOGUE</p>
